{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The notehead type indicates shapes other than the open and closed ovals associated with note durations."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SQ","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/SH","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNote"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnote\/notehead-swift.struct"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Notehead"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The smufl attribute can be used to specify a particular notehead, allowing application interoperability"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"without requiring every SMuFL glyph to have a MusicXML element equivalent. This attribute can be used either"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the “other” value, or to refine a specific notehead value such as “cluster”. Noteheads in the SMuFL Note"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name noteheads and Note name noteheads supplement ranges (U+E150–U+E1AF and U+EEE0–U+EEFF) should not use the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"smufl attribute or the “other” value, but instead use the notehead-text element."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For the enclosed shapes, the default is to be hollow for half notes and longer, and filled otherwise. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"filled attribute ca